{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And he was there with YHWH.</b> Forty days — from the third rising of the dawn on the twenty-ninth of Av until the rising of the dawn on the tenth of Tishrei. And if you ask: from where did Moses know when it was day and when it was night, given that they are equal above, as it is written ״ונהורא עמיה שריה״ (and the light dwells with Him), and it says ״גם חושך לא יחשיך ממך ולילה כיום יאיר כחשכה כאורה״ (even darkness does not darken from You, and night as day illuminates, darkness as light) — rather, when HaShem taught him the written Torah, he knew it was day, and when He taught him the oral Torah, he knew it was night; and furthermore, when he sees the moon, stars, and constellations kneeling and bowing before HaShem, he knew it was day, and when he sees the sun kneeling and bowing, he knew it was night." "<b>And he wrote on the tablets.</b> HaShem wrote — and the proof is in the section of Ekev. Furthermore, it is written above: וכתבתי על הלוחות (and I wrote on the tablets)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The abbreviation במ׳ is resolved as 'forty days' based on context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:56.434124099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}